# Pronunciation scoring HTTP client

Contract: [`docs/pronunciation-score-api.md`](../../docs/pronunciation-score-api.md).

- Settings store the **full** `POST` URL (`speechScoreApiUrl`). Fetch that URL as-is; do not join `/api/v2/pronunciation/score` at request time. Do not rewrite already-saved `/api/v1/...` URLs.
- Do not add a `/health` client, settings “test connection”, or `SpeechScoreHealthResponse`.
- Send `audio`, `reference_text`, `reference_duration`, and `language` as `multipart/form-data` with `X-API-Key`.
- `speechScoreProsodyBasis` defaults to `naturalness` (both Echo and Shadowing text + duration only). When set to `match`, both Echo and Shadowing may send `reference_audio` + `reference_audio_roles=prosody` or `reference_prosody_profile` (JSON string) — never both. Echo keys profiles by `mediaId:segmentId`; Shadowing by `mediaId:<ordered segment ids joined with |>` (single-segment Shadowing shares the Echo key). Shadowing canonical clip: first practice segment `sourceStartTime` → last subtitle `endTime`; canonical duration: sum of per-segment subtitle durations; clip wall-clock > 60 s → silent degrade. Missing media/clip → silent degrade (omit both).
- Cache profiles in IndexedDB (`referenceProsodyProfile`); exclude from backup; clear on `deleteMedia`. On 422 after a cached profile, delete that key and do not retry in the same call.
- Response may include `prosody_naturalness`, `prosody_match`, and `details.reference_prosody_profile`. Persist them on `PronunciationScore`. UI shows `prosody` + four breakdown dims; when `prosody_match` is present, use match-oriented labels (贴近). Do **not** show top-level `prosody_match`, naturalness, match_breakdown, or profile.
- Word-level errors use three disjoint positioned lists: `missing_words` (`word` + `ref_index` + `char_*`), `misread_words` (`expected`/`actual` + ref/hyp indices + char spans + optional `start`/`end`), and `extra_words` (`word` + `hyp_index` + `char_*`). Char spans use the LF coordinate system (`details.reference_newline === "lf"`): LF-normalize local reference before `slice`; use `details.transcript` for hyp spans; do not rely on a returned `details.reference_text`. UI highlights by char span on reference/transcript; only playable misreads seek recording audio.
- Keep on-demand scoring only; 60 s / 10 MB local rejection; types in `src/types/models.ts` must stay aligned with the contract.
